{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgXuDM7aXnAAAMfvxBBAw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draw anything, this is how I read the request.\n\nQuestion: which screens does a Fernhouse customer pass through to start a return, and where do they choose?\nOutcome: the product team can follow a return from the order list to a confirmed return and see where the 30 day window ends it.\nDials: Balanced detail, a Mixed audience with the app's own words and a Laptop reading distance.\n\nSettled by your text:\n- The app and returns doc give the order list, then the order detail listing each item with its price and delivery date, with Start a return under the items.\n- The reasons are Damaged, Wrong size, Not as shown and Changed my mind.\n- A drop-off point is picked from a map of the 5 nearest points. A courier pickup takes a date in the next 3 working days.\n- The confirmation shows a QR code to scan at the drop-off point or hand to the courier, and emails it.\n- Returns are open for 30 days after delivery, and after that the app shows Contact support.\n\nLeft out: the free pickup over 100 euros, a proposal under review. Nothing after the confirmation is drawn.\n\nAssumed, each corrected by a no:\n- The reader is the product team.\n- The 30 day check follows the order detail, so Contact support is the exit for a customer past 30 days.\n- The email sits in the confirmation's body, not in a node of its own.\n- Balanced detail, a Mixed audience and a Laptop distance.\n\nOutline, 9 nodes and 9 connectors:\n- Order list, the start\n- Order detail, with the items, prices, delivery dates and Start a return in its body\n- Within 30 days after delivery?, the decision, with No leading to Contact support and Yes to the reasons\n- Contact support, an exit drawn below the main row\n- Pick a reason, with the four reasons in its body\n- Drop-off or courier pickup?, the second decision\n- Choose a drop-off point, with the map of 5 nearest points in its body\n- Book a courier pickup, with the date in the next 3 working days in its body\n- Return confirmed, the goal, with the QR code and the email in its body\n\nTwo framings:\n- **Happy path with the exit beside it:** the main row runs from the order list to the confirmation and Contact support sits below. It reads fastest and costs the sight of every other exit.\n- **State map of every exit:** it shows each way a return can stop. The sources name only one exit, so this adds nothing a reader needs.\n- **Recommended:** the happy path, because the sources give one early exit and the reader's question is about the path.\n\nThe look:\n- It runs left to right in three zones, Find the order, Request the return and Done, each with notes saying where it starts and ends.\n- The 30 day decision takes the accent, with the reason \"returns can end early here\". The confirmation is named the goal and is not styled.\n- The board is titled \"Start a return\", with a source line naming the app, the returns doc and the left-out proposal.\n\nStill open: none.\n\nIs this the right reading of the board?"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":917,"cache_read_input_tokens":87658,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":917},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"131bd65f-4ad0-4e3b-872a-7716b76fae6e","uuid":"707134a9-b725-49e1-a92b-c0bac1de2386","timestamp":"2026-10-30T05:52:36.153Z","request_id":"req_011CgXuDLoixGD9Rvb6J6ipz"}
